cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Results are provisional (pre-defence)."
type: software
title: "sp-respiratory-admissions-forecast: daily forecasting of respiratory hospital admissions in São Paulo city, 1 to 30 days ahead, with seven models under one temporal validation protocol"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/matheusmmmp/sp-respiratory-admissions-forecast"
url: "https://sp-respiratory-admissions-forecast.streamlit.app"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pereira"
    given-names: "Matheus de Medeiros"
    affiliation: "Programa de Pós-Graduação em Ciência da Computação (PPGCC), Universidade Federal de Santa Catarina (UFSC)"
keywords:
  - time-series forecasting
  - public health
  - hospital admissions
  - air pollution
  - PM2.5
  - SIH/SUS
  - XGBoost
  - LSTM
  - SARIMAX
  - INGARCH
  - GAM
abstract: >-
  Code, aggregated daily data and identified run artefacts for forecasting the daily
  count of hospital admissions with a respiratory principal diagnosis (ICD-10 J00-J99)
  among residents of the municipality of São Paulo, Brazil, 2019-2024, 1 to 30 days
  ahead. Seven models (Naive, Seasonal Naive, XGBoost, LSTM, SARIMAX, GAM-NB,
  INGARCH-NB) are evaluated under the same rolling-origin protocol (4 folds x 180 test
  days, 5 seeds for the stochastic models) with paired Diebold-Mariano tests and Holm
  correction. Environmental covariates come from CETESB/QUALAR (main source) and CAMS
  (alternative source). Derived from a master's dissertation at PPGCC/UFSC, advised by
  Renato Fileto and co-advised by Simone S. Werner. All results are provisional
  (pre-defence).
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "PM2.5 e internações respiratórias (CID-10 J00-J99), município de São Paulo, 2019-2024 (master's dissertation, in preparation)"
    authors:
